<section class="rule"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Illustrative scenarios</div><h2>How value could be created—shown honestly.</h2><p class="lead">The scenarios below are hypothetical models. They exist to make our methods concrete, not to imply completed client engagements.</p>
<div class="grid-2">
<div class="card proof"><div class="badge amber">Illustrative scenario — hypothetical</div><h3>Mid-market professional-services firm</h3><p class="muted">A 400-person advisory firm applies the Readiness Diagnostic and discovers its constraint is not model access but unstructured knowledge capture. A bounded pilot restructures proposal development around a retrieval-augmented workflow, governed by a Pilot Passport with explicit quality and confidentiality controls, before any firm-wide rollout decision.</p></div>
<div class="card proof"><div class="badge amber">Illustrative scenario — hypothetical</div><h3>Regional manufacturer</h3><p class="muted">A manufacturer under margin pressure uses the Human-Augmented Business Model Canvas to separate decisions that can be automated (scheduling, anomaly detection) from those that must stay human-led (supplier negotiation, safety judgment). The resulting portfolio sequences three pilots by value, feasibility and workforce readiness rather than by vendor enthusiasm.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="rule"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">The Trouvus operating standard</div><h2>Designed for impact. Governed for certainty.</h2><div class="grid-3">
<div class="card proof"><div class="badge violet">Research-grounded methodology</div><h3>Academic rigor, enterprise relevance</h3><p class="muted">Decisions are built on published research, established business-model methods and explicit evidence—not vendor enthusiasm.</p></div>
<div class="card proof"><div class="badge green">Governed execution</div><h3>Pre-committed pilot metrics</h3><p class="muted">Every initiative begins with an explicit hypothesis, accountable owner, risk controls and a scale, iterate or stop decision rule.</p></div>
<div class="card proof"><div class="badge amber">Capability retention</div><h3>Human agency at the core</h3><p class="muted">Systems are designed to remove routine toil while strengthening leadership judgment, workforce competence and institutional learning.</p></div>
